contracts/VERIFIER.md:32:When this install has a host build budget (`seats/host-budget.json` exists and seat launch/probe/one-shot PATHs include `seats/bin`), every build and test the surface leads you to run goes through the shim, regardless of whether the seat harness is `pi`, `claude-code`, or `codex`; never call the raw tool by absolute path, by a PATH that skips `seats/bin`, or by any other escape hatch. Build caches are shared under the host lock by default. Per-worktree cache isolation is allowed only with a written reason on the bead, because isolation multiplies disk and compile load.
